/** Provides what helix-raylib adds to raylib 5.5's API, written as raylib writes its own, so `Raylib` is raylib's alone. Imported apart,
	as `Raymath` is: `import helix.raylib.Extras.*;`.

	It holds the loads, requests and writes a page can't wait for, each `...Async` in place of raylib's call that is done when it returns
	(`LoadTextureAsync` for `LoadTexture`, `ToggleFullscreenAsync` for `ToggleFullscreen`): raylib's call doesn't compile, naming the one
	here (docs/DECISIONS.md 24). And it holds what a game needs from the device and the page that raylib has no call for: the safe area
	around a notch, the options the program was started with, the screen's orientation, what the device is, whether the window can close
	or go fullscreen, and the device's tilt.

	Each is answered by helix-platform, on every target; where a target has no such thing the answer says so (no tilt natively, the
	whole window as the safe area on a desktop) rather than the call failing to compile, so a game needs no `#if js` for any of them.
	Each `...Async` call answers at a later poll, never during the call: `done` once it is granted, `failed` with the reason when it is
	refused, logged as raylib's warning would be when `failed` is omitted. */
